@anon.879c592214345ca999bafaa324406990.846 = private unnamed_addr constant [502 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for non-empty function stub bodies.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AStub files are never executed at runtime; they should be thought of as\0A\22data files\22 for type checkers or IDEs. Function bodies are redundant\0Afor this purpose.\0A\0A## Example\0A```pyi\0Adef double(x: int) -> int:\0A    return x * 2\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```pyi\0Adef double(x: int) -> int: ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Typing documentation - Writing and Maintaining Stub Files](https://typing.python.org/en/latest/guides/writing_stubs.html)\0A", align 1
