@anon.879c592214345ca999bafaa324406990.923 = private unnamed_addr constant [523 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for a re-defined slot in a subclass.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIf a class defines a slot also defined in a base class, the\0Ainstance variable defined by the base class slot is inaccessible\0A(except by retrieving its descriptor directly from the base class).\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aclass Base:\0A    __slots__ = (\22a\22, \22b\22)\0A\0A\0Aclass Subclass(Base):\0A    __slots__ = (\22a\22, \22d\22)  # slot \22a\22 redefined\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aclass Base:\0A    __slots__ = (\22a\22, \22b\22)\0A\0A\0Aclass Subclass(Base):\0A    __slots__ = \22d\22\0A```\0A", align 1
